# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model artefacts - DELIBERATELY COMMITTED
#
# These were ignored at first, on the usual reasoning: binary files do not diff,
# and "make train" regenerates them in about ten seconds.
#
# That reasoning stopped holding once the Streamlit app was deployed to a free
# tier with roughly 1 GB of memory. Fitting LightGBM is the memory-hungry step,
# not serving it, so a cold container that has to train three models on first
# request is the most likely thing to fall over - and it would fall over for a
# visitor, not for us. All three artefacts together are 2.3 MB.
#
# Trading 2.3 MB of repository size for a deploy that cannot OOM on first load
# is the right way round. Left here as a comment rather than deleted, because
# the original reasoning is still correct in a project without a 1 GB ceiling.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ml/models/*.joblib
# ml/models/*.metrics.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated data
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored. The CSVs are around 23 MB, they are deterministic
# from a fixed seed, and a client cloning this repo should be able to open the
# Power BI file without running Python first. If the data ever grows past what
# git is comfortable with, ignore data/*.csv and ship a release artefact
# instead - but that is a decision to take on purpose, not by default.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Power BI
#
# .pbix is a binary package. It does not diff, it does not merge, and two
# people editing it produces a conflict nobody can resolve. Keep the report
# definition in BUILD_GUIDE.md and the measures in version-controlled DAX,
# which is the whole reason those files exist.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pbix
*.pbit
*.pbip
.pbi/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
